        "worksFor": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "Moidas"
        }
      }
    </script>
  </slot>
  <style>
    :root {
      --cv-font-body: 'Noto Serif SC', 'Source Serif 4', serif;
    }
  </style>

  <div class="container">
    <header>
      <h1>Hongkun Wang</h1>
      <div class="contact-info">
        <span class="contact-item"><a href="mailto:me@wilboerht.cn">me@wilboerht.cn</a></span>
        <span class="contact-item"><a href="tel:+8618721400154">+86 187 2140 0154</a></span>
        <span class="contact-item"><a href="https://github.com/Wilboerht" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a></span>
        <span class="contact-item"><a href="https://www.wilboerht.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">wilboerht.com</a></span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Experience</h2>
      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-header">
          <span class="entry-org"
            >Moidas | NIHPLOD Greater China Division — Digital Development Manager</span
          >
          <span class="entry-date">Oct 2025 - Present</span>
        </div>
        <p class="entry-role-detail">
          Joined as an intern in Oct 2025 and worked full-time before graduation; converted to full-time in Jul 2026, reporting directly to the brand lead.
        </p>
        <ul class="project-points">
          <li>Owned planning and delivery of the brand's Greater China digital product portfolio — 6+ core systems including the official website, WeChat AI customer service, authenticity verification, and AI skincare advisor.</li>
          <li>Established AI-assisted development workflows and design standards, reducing average delivery cycles by over 50% while ensuring parallel multi-project delivery.</li>
          <li>Acted as technical lead interfacing with product and marketing teams, establishing rapid iteration mechanisms that supported online business growth.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-header">
          <span class="entry-org"
            >Shanghai Lingang Jinghong Security Technology Development Co., Ltd. — R&amp;D Intern</span
          >
          <span class="entry-date">Jul 2025 - Sep 2025</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="project-points">
          <li>Independently delivered the company website end-to-end, from architecture and UI/UX design to production deployment.</li>
          <li>Completed an internal MVP campus patrol management platform via secondary development on the Unitree robot dog SDK, validating product feasibility.</li>
          <li>Drove the company's first internal adoption of AI Q&amp;A tools and engaged with Baidu's official Enterprise Q&amp;A team on business collaboration.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Projects</h2>

      <div class="project-entry">
        <div class="entry-header">
          <span class="project-name">NIHPLOD China Official Digital Platform (Portfolio)</span>
          <span class="entry-date">Nov 2025 - Present</span>
        </div>
        <div class="project-meta">
          Live: <a
            href="https://www.nihplod.cn"
            target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.nihplod.cn</a
          >, <a href="https://advisor.nihplod.cn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >advisor.nihplod.cn</a
          >, <a href="https://ba.nihplod.cn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >ba.nihplod.cn</a
          >, etc.
        </div>
        <p class="project-abstract">
          As technical lead, drove the brand's Greater China digital product matrix from 0 to 1 — architecture design and compliant launch — spanning 6+ systems: the official e-commerce site, unified authentication (SSO), AI skincare advisor, WeChat AI customer service, WeChat mini-program store, and the authorization &amp; verification platform (detailed below), with 170K+ lines of hand-written code and 1,400+ automated test cases delivered in total.
        </p>
        <ul class="project-points">
          <li>
            <strong>Compliance &amp; Operations Governance:</strong> Led ICP filing, privacy policy and user agreement drafting, and data compliance review to ensure compliant launches across systems; dynamically adjusted server resources based on traffic to optimize costs.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="project-entry">
        <div class="entry-header">
          <span class="project-name">NIHPLOD Official E-Commerce &amp; Unified Authentication Platform</span>
          <span class="entry-date">Nov 2025 - Present</span>
        </div>
        <div class="project-meta">
          Live: <a
            href="https://www.nihplod.cn"
            target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.nihplod.cn</a
          >
        </div>
        <ul class="project-points">
          <li>
            <strong>E-Commerce Loop:</strong> Built the brand's e-commerce main site with Next.js 16 + Prisma + PostgreSQL, covering dual-channel payments (WeChat Pay / Alipay) and refunds (idempotent async notifications), SF Express logistics, and membership points &amp; coupon systems; aggregated multi-channel identities (WeChat, Douyin, phone OTP) into a unified account system — 121 API routes, 36 data models, and 824 test cases across the site.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Unified Authentication (SSO):</strong> Built a self-hosted OAuth 2.0 / OIDC SSO — the main site acts as Authorization Server issuing RS256 JWTs, fully implementing the authorize / token / userinfo / introspect / revoke / end-session endpoints with PKCE, DPoP, and TOTP two-factor authentication; packaged and published npm SDKs (@nihplod/sso-sdk / @nihplod/sso-verify) for minute-level sub-project integration, with Token Introspection + Backchannel Logout for cross-domain SSO and global sign-out.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Security Hardening:</strong> Supports secret rotation, token revocation (RFC 7009), and multi-instance blacklist sharing for an operable and auditable auth system.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Interactive Experience:</strong> Implemented multi-step skincare ritual guides and immersive brand storytelling using Framer Motion + View Transitions, with integrated product drawer and cart synchronization, fully responsive across devices.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="project-entry">
        <div class="entry-header">
          <span class="project-name">AI Skincare Advisor</span>
          <span class="entry-date">Jan 2026 - Present</span>
        </div>
        <div class="project-meta">
          Live: <a href="https://advisor.nihplod.cn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >advisor.nihplod.cn</a
          >
        </div>
        <ul class="project-points">
          <li>
            <strong>AI Skin Analysis &amp; Personalized Recommendations:</strong> Integrated qwen-vl / deepseek-vl vision LLMs for dual-channel (questionnaire + facial scan) skin analysis, with a custom rule engine scoring products against 8 skin-type personas and multi-channel e-commerce attribution links; led model integration and core API development, lifting consultation conversion by 30%.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>AI Cost Engineering:</strong> Designed circuit breakers with daily/monthly token budget cutoffs, persisted per-call billing, and a model whitelist with fallback for AI invocations — fixing a duplicate-billing risk caused by 5xx retries; user reports follow 90-day rolling retention with hot/cold tiered archiving (desensitized summaries in the cold tier).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Human-AI Handoff Pipeline:</strong> Designed a server-to-server authenticated API that transfers advisor sessions to WeChat human agents with full context (session_id passthrough), ensuring service continuity.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="project-entry">
        <div class="entry-header">
          <span class="project-name">WeChat AI Customer Service</span>
          <span class="entry-date">Aug 2026 - Present</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="project-points">
          <li>
            <strong>Multi-Entry Messaging Gateway &amp; Multi-Turn Sessions:</strong> Built with FastAPI + Redis + the DeepSeek LLM, unifying three message entry points (WeCom customer service, WeCom app, and WeChat Official Account); implemented on-demand segmented knowledge-base injection, multi-turn sessions with user skincare profiles, guided order inquiries, and smart human handoff (keyword detection + service-hour windows + sticky agent assignment).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Compliance &amp; Quality Assurance:</strong> Built-in advertising-law prohibited-word filtering and PII export/deletion endpoints (PIPL compliance); self-hosted on Linux + Nginx, backed by 340+ test cases (including 34 golden regression cases against the live LLM).
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="project-entry">
        <div class="entry-header">
          <span class="project-name">WeChat Mini-Program Store</span>
          <span class="entry-date">May 2026 - Present</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="project-points">
          <li>
            <strong>Full-Stack Commerce Loop:</strong> Built with uni-app + Vue 3 + Express 5 + Prisma + PostgreSQL (mini-program/H5 dual-end plus a standalone admin console), covering the full pipeline of WeChat Pay V3, refund chain, SF Express logistics, and SMS notifications.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Engineering &amp; Security:</strong> Implemented RBAC, audit logging, and multi-tier rate limiting — 26 data models, 191 automated tests (including concurrent-ordering tests), deployed via multi-stage Docker builds.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="project-entry">
        <div class="entry-header">
          <span class="project-name">NIHPLOD Brand Authorization &amp; Verification Platform</span>
          <span class="entry-date">Apr 2026 - Present</span>
        </div>
        <div class="project-meta">
          Live: <a href="https://ba.nihplod.cn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >ba.nihplod.cn</a
          >
        </div>
        <ul class="project-points">
          <li>
            <strong>Authorization Review &amp; Anti-Counterfeit Certificates:</strong> Built the dealer authorization system with Next.js + Prisma + PostgreSQL, implementing a multi-level review workflow (application → auditor review → manager issuance); Canvas-based synthesis of anti-counterfeit certificates with e-seal and dynamic QR codes (PNG/PDF download).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Public Verification &amp; Security:</strong> Public authenticity verification with three-tier fallback matching (exact → prefix → fuzzy, accelerated by pg_trgm indexes) and a counterfeit-report ticketing system; hardened with JWT blacklisting, database-persisted rate limiting, and full audit logging.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="project-entry">
        <div class="entry-header">
          <span class="project-name"
            >Shanghai Lingang Jinghong Security Technology Website System</span
          >
          <span class="entry-date">Jul 2025 - Sep 2025</span>
        </div>
        <div class="project-meta">
          Independently delivered (full-stack) · Live: <a
            href="https://www.lingangjh.com"
            target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.lingangjh.com</a
          >
        </div>
        <ul class="project-points">
          <li>
            <strong>Full-Stack Development &amp; Design Delivery:</strong> Independently built the company website end-to-end with Next.js plus a CMS backend for autonomous content management, and independently designed the visual system and interaction prototypes in Figma — first-screen load under 1.5s, fully responsive across devices.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>AI Q&amp;A &amp; Security Architecture:</strong> Locally deployed the Wenxin/Qwen LLM-powered Q&amp;A assistant (Weknora) with a RAG retrieval pipeline, achieving answer accuracy above 85%; implemented JWT authentication, RLS data isolation, and CSP policies for data security and access control.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

